# Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the React + Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (version ^2.0.0) using npm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the resolved dependency tree

### 2. Code Integration
Modified `client/src/App.jsx`:
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the app JSX, positioned alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I:
1. Fetched the latest installation instructions from the Vercel documentation
2. Identified this as a React + Vite project (confirmed by package.json and vite.config.js)
3. Used the React-specific installation path: `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
4. Added the component to the main App.jsx file, following the same pattern as the existing Analytics integration

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build` - no errors)
✅ Linter checked (pre-existing errors unrelated to this change)
✅ Lock files updated properly
✅ Code follows existing project patterns (placed next to Analytics component)

## Next Steps

To see Speed Insights data:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for your project
3. After deployment and user visits, view performance metrics in the dashboard

The SpeedInsights component will automatically start collecting Core Web Vitals data (LCP, FID, CLS, etc.) once deployed to Vercel.
